    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0115" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg35"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Infante to Mr.
                            Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Chile</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-09"><hi rendition="#italic">October 9,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am in receipt of instructions
                    from the Government of Chile directing me to take such steps as may be required
                    to obtain for the commander and officers of the training ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">General <pb facs="0116" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/>
                        Baquedano</hi>, at present anchored in the bay of New York, permission to
                    deposit in the Washington Monument, on behalf of the people of Chile, a plaque
                    commemorative of that illustrious leader of the American independence and
                    founder of the Republic of the United States of America.</p>
                <p>I shall be thankful if your excellency will kindly apply to appropriate
                    authorities for the permission to place the said plaque, provided there should
                    be no objection on your part.</p>
                <p>It is for me a pleasure, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Infante.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
